  "name": "Hamilton cycles appearing early in an edge process",
  "description": "construct() -> a permutation of vertices 0..23, describing a Hamilton cycle with implicit closing edge. Score is the largest one-based arrival index of its edges in the pinned uniformly shuffled complete-graph edge list. Minimize that prefix index. The evaluator certifies presence, not absence of all earlier Hamilton cycles. One complete-edge permutation on 24 vertices, locally shuffled with random.Random(614), replaces an asymptotic random ensemble. Each score is an upper bound on this sample’s true hitting time, not proof that it is earliest.",
